    <statement><p>Which is a parametric equation for the curve <m>36 = \left(x-3\right)^{2}+\left(y+8\right)^{2}</m>?</p>
<p><var form="buttons">
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(3+6\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right),6\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-8\right)</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(6\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-8,3+6\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)\right)</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(36\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-8,3+36\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)\right)</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(3+36\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right),36\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-8\right)</m></p>
</li>
</var></p>
</statement>
    <solution><m>(3, -8)</m>.  Using the parametric representation of a circle we get <m>c(t) = \left(3+6\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right),6\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-8\right)</m>.


</solution>
